<p>The application that converts is on the homepage: <a href="/become-a-dealer/">Become a Dealer</a>. Check Shiloh. Tell us what you build now and what you used to sell. That is enough to start the call.</p>

<h2>Two shops we talk to every week</h2>
<p><strong>You used to sell Kraftmaid, Medallion, or a similar stock or semi-custom program.</strong> Clients now want more modification, a better box, inset, a paint they cannot get off a restricted deck. Shiloh is the step-up line: WW Wood, Dudley, Missouri, all-plywood, dovetail drawers, ~6-week lead. You are not asking your crew to become a custom shop overnight.</p>
<p><strong>You already build custom.</strong> Factory Shiloh covers the jobs that should not consume the bench — paint, inset, furniture vanities, a predictable lead. You keep true custom for the one-offs. Shiloh is not a replacement for the shop. It is the line you sell when the shop should stay on the work that only you can build.</p>

<h2>Shiloh-only is a real path</h2>
<p>Six public brands, not five: Shiloh, Eclipse, Aspect, Vistora, Pronorm, US Stone. You can open <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh</a> alone. Face-frame and inset, six inset styles, Sherwin-Williams custom paint, White Oak and rift-cut without an upcharge. Eclipse is the same factory if you later want frameless — see <a href="/guides/face-frame-vs-frameless/">face-frame vs frameless</a>. You do not need Pronorm, stone, or closets on the first order.</p>

<h2>Territory, not a locator</h2>
<p>Shiloh is a WW Wood line. Pinnacle manages it across Arizona, California, Colorado, Idaho, Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, Oregon, Utah, and Washington. We do not list dealers and we do not send homeowners to a store. Apply; we tell you what is open. Map: <a href="/guides/protected-dealer-territories/">protected dealer territories</a>.</p>

<p>Nevara is a dealer-only WW Wood SKU. It is not on this site.</p>

<p><a href="/become-a-dealer/">Apply for Shiloh</a> — check the Shiloh box, note custom and any prior stock or semi-custom program, submit.</p>

